A||||3||LuckyTheyWereEverMade||Help! Axle won't pull out of automatic transmission||||1||
Z||000000||LuckyTheyWereEverMade||03-27-2001||12:00 AM||||I have a bad transmission seal in my TH-125c automatic transmission.  The car is a 1984 sport coupe with the 4cylinder engine.<BR>The passenger side toe rod and A-arm ball joint have been seperated and the brake is hanging on a wire.<P>But try as hard as I can, the damn axle won't come out when I pry on it with a variety of tools ranging from screwdrivers to the spare tire lug wrench.  <P>The driver's side axle was a real *****  to pull, but the passenger side is unbelievable! It just wont budge.  Prying is not going to get it out.<P>Both of the axles just popped out of my parts car and it's an '84 also.   Why is there such a difference?  How can I get the stupid axle out of the god damn tranny?<P>Please Help! ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Fierowrecker||03-27-2001||12:02 AM||||You need the tool...<BR>It is a slide hammer with a right angle fork...<BR>crash...<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||V8Fiero||03-27-2001||01:40 AM||||Had the same problem on mine. 84 auto. I mustve cussed and sweared for over an hour. I got mine loose by laying underneath the car with a flat bar up from the bottom between the two and hitting it with a hammer. Be carefull not to bang the tranny up. I also had a hell of a time getting the new axle in after I got the old one out.<P>Good luck. It WILL come out......eventually. <BR>I suggest taking a break...maybe even a day, and return to it again.<P>Scott||||reg||1
Z||000003||LuckyTheyWereEverMade||03-28-2001||02:10 AM||||The axle is out.  <P>I used a slide hammer with a "crow's foot" widget on the end of it.  It took about 30 or 40 blasts of the slide hammer to do the trick, but it's out now.<P>The only problem is that slide hammers are expensive . . .Ouch!||||reg||1
